Z||000005||mrfiero||02-12-2001||07:22 PM||||I don't know about the hitches up on eBay, but the Fiero Store hitch has worked well for me.  I have towed several cars (mostly Fieros) with it behind an '88 GT.  I'm sure I over-extended the tow rating, but no ill effects so far (3 cross country trips!).  <P>I towed a 2000 Saturn from Oregon to Maine and averaged 15MPG at 70MPH.<P>At any rate......I would say the $75 asking price on those eBay hitches is a bargain.   ||||reg||10
Z||000006||gabriel||02-13-2001||05:13 AM||||Try here:<P>        <A HREF="http://www.outlawperformance.org" TARGET=_blank>www.outlawperformance.org</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||02-13-2001||10:51 AM||||Wow!  I didn't want to tow more than a motorcycle trailer. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  My luggage or camping gear or any gear for that matter fills my car up too soon especially with a passenger.  The additional room would be greatly appreciated by my friends and they wouldn't complain about the limited space any more.||||reg||1
Z||000008||pherder||02-13-2001||12:22 PM||||I think you will find that the fiberglass, the trailer hitch, and other parts and pieces that some Fiero suppliers sell are made by what is called Outlaw Performance (AKA GRM Fabrications ... used to be on the "East" coast of Florida by the Kennedy Space Center), now of St. Petersburg, FL. (on the "West" coast of Florida.)<P>The Fiero Store just buys the pieces, adds a reseller's profit margin to it and resells it to us.<P>I am one who got one of the trailer hitches in the latest round of eBay auctions.<P>Ended up costing $95 (75 auction price with $20 shipping).  It is still less than the web page cost of $100 + shipping from them or the $150 cost + shipping from The Fiero Store.<P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com||||reg||1
Z||000009||TheFiero64||02-13-2001||05:57 PM||||I've always wanted to make a trailer out of the back of a Fiero. Then when I go on long trips I can pack everything in the trailer and have plenty of room in my Fiero. It would look good in shows too. Draw attention.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
